  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Opportunities for Mainstreaming Inclusive Development</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the project is to increase the participation of women in society, through more female voices in community institutions; to create economic opportunities and livelihoods for women and through a peacebuilding component that focuses in particular on reducing conflicts around natural resource management. The project builds on the past NL-funded Afghanistan Community-Led Economic Stability (ACES) project and will be implemented in 8 pr ovinces: Badakhshan, Takhar, Kunduz, Baghlan, Samangan, Bamyan, Parwan and Daykundi, where AKF has a has a large network.</narrative>
  </description>
